@startuml
title Implemented Session Authentication and Lifecycle
actor User
participant "Angular AuthService" as UI
participant "Security / Auth API" as API
participant "Spring Session JDBC" as Sessions
database PostgreSQL as DB
UI -> API : GET /api/v1/auth/csrf
API -> Sessions : Materialize session-bound CSRF
Sessions -> DB : IMMEDIATE persistence
API --> UI : 200 envelope: masked csrfToken / X-CSRF-TOKEN
User -> UI : Submit exact email/password
UI -> API : POST /api/v1/auth/login + SESSION cookie + X-CSRF-TOKEN
API -> Sessions : Validate masked CSRF before unsafe behavior
API -> DB : Canonical credential lookup
API -> API : PBKDF2-HMAC-SHA256 verification\n600,000 iterations / versioned encoder
alt Unknown / wrong / disabled account
  API --> UI : Generic 401 / 1001; no new activation
else Valid enabled supported role
  API -> Sessions : Identifier rotation + invalidate old CSRF
  API -> Sessions : Save credential-free context attribute
  Sessions -> DB : Flush rotated identifier/context before output
  API -> DB : Lock account; recheck enabled/role/auth_version\nactivate auth_session_activity; commit
  API --> UI : 200 minimal id/email/role + rotated SESSION
  UI -> API : GET /api/v1/auth/csrf for fresh masked token
end
UI -> API : GET /api/v1/auth/me (startup/user interaction; no polling)
API -> DB : Check session / current account / version / strict deadline
API -> DB : Guarded monotonic activity update at handler admission
API --> UI : 200 minimal identity, or 401 / 503
User -> UI : Sign out
UI -> API : POST /api/v1/auth/logout + cookie + CSRF
API -> Sessions : Synchronous session invalidation
Sessions -> DB : Delete parent; cascade attributes/activity
API --> UI : 200/null + SESSION deletion with original scope
UI -> UI : Clear private views; bootstrap anonymous CSRF separately
note over UI, DB
SESSION: host-only /api/v1, HttpOnly, Lax, browser lifetime.
Secure=true production; explicit local profile permits HTTP.
Strict 30-minute idle deadline; bootstrap/health/logout do not renew.
Account changes increment auth_version; old sessions never revive.
Required lifecycle persistence precedes success; transactions are separate.
Before-commit store failures: generic 503/3002.
After commitment: safe operational reporting / possible transport termination.
Confirmed transitions survive subsequent CSRF-refresh failure.
No automatic unsafe replay or authentication browser storage.
end note
@enduml
